NOTE ON psycopg (LGPL-3.0-only). This is the one copyleft dependency and the
only one worth a paragraph. twicetold-npc does not vendor, modify, or
redistribute psycopg: it is declared in requirements.txt and installed from
PyPI by the operator, and this project links against it as a separate work.
Apache-2.0 for this repository's own source is unaffected. An integrator who
chooses to REDISTRIBUTE psycopg inside a bundled artifact takes on LGPL-3.0's
obligations for that copy (notably the ability to relink against a modified
psycopg) — which is their packaging decision, not this project's. Anyone who
prefers to avoid it entirely can swap the driver: all SQL is hand-written and
confined to app/db.py, with no ORM in the way.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEVELOPMENT-TIME TOOLS (not dependencies of the running service)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MCP for Unity (CoplayDev/unity-mcp)
  Referenced by unity/Packages/manifest.json and resolved into
  unity/Packages/ by Unity's package manager. Gitignored, never committed.
  Editor-only: it is not part of a build and ships with nothing.

Postgres MCP Pro (crystaldba/postgres-mcp)
  Run from its own isolated uv-managed venv; not in requirements.txt.
  A development-machine convenience; nothing in the service depends on it.

pgvector/pgvector:pg16 (Docker image)
  The local development database. PostgreSQL License + pgvector's PostgreSQL
  License. Pulled at runtime by docker compose; not redistributed here.

python:3.14-slim (Docker base image)
  The base image the API image is built FROM by docker compose. Python Software
  Foundation License, plus the Debian slim base's own package licenses. Pulled
  at build time; the resulting API image is never published (see the psycopg
  note above for why a prebuilt image is deliberately not shipped).
